+"""Where every pre-P09 native assertion stands on the one presentation (C44).
+
+Each legacy check id maps to a kind and its targets:
+  x  exercised: the named v2 checks assert the same requirement on the C44 bundle (their results bind the gate).
+  s  self: the legacy driver itself runs on the one presentation through legacy_v2 (run_on_v2.py <cNN> legacy).
+  p  ported: the requirement was added to the named v2 check in C44 (a new fact in that driver's record).
+  r  retired: the requirement concerns the legacy shell or a surface the one presentation does not have (D059: the
+     prototype is the specification; D060: no import from the alpha; the owner on 2026-10-31: the application is
+     driven by the new UI alone). Where the behaviour survives in the core, the retirement names the suite that holds
+     it (crates/desktop-core/tests/<name>, run by the gate's core-fixtures step); that suite result does not stand in
+     for a native assertion and the map says so.
+The note says which fact of the target carries the requirement. The gate (acceptance_c44.py) fails when an exercised,
+self or ported target is missing or failing on this bundle, or a retirement has no reason.
+"""
